<section class="container article-field-resource" id="appointment-setting-cost-example" aria-labelledby="appointment-setting-cost-heading">
  <h2 id="appointment-setting-cost-heading">What does each meeting actually cost?</h2>
  <p>Say you’re comparing a $4,000 monthly retainer with a quote of $250 per booking. Divide the full bill by the number of meetings at each stage.</p>
  <table class="article-cost-example">
    <caption>Example for one month. All prices are in US dollars.</caption>
    <thead><tr><th scope="col">Measure</th><th scope="col">Retainer</th><th scope="col">Pay per booking</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><th scope="row">Total bill</th><td>$4,000</td><td>$3,000</td></tr>
      <tr><th scope="row">Meetings booked</th><td>10</td><td>12</td></tr>
      <tr><th scope="row">Meetings held</th><td>8</td><td>6</td></tr>
      <tr><th scope="row">Meetings sales accepted</th><td>6</td><td>3</td></tr>
      <tr><th scope="row">Cost per booking</th><td>$400</td><td>$250</td></tr>
      <tr><th scope="row">Cost per held meeting</th><td>$500</td><td>$500</td></tr>
      <tr><th scope="row">Cost per sales-accepted meeting</th><td>$667</td><td>$1,000</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p><strong>Follow the pay-per-booking math:</strong> 12 bookings at $250 each cost $3,000. Sales accepts 3. That’s $3,000 ÷ 3 = <strong>$1,000 per accepted meeting</strong>. The retainer comes to about <strong>$667 per accepted meeting</strong>.</p>
  <p><a href="#quote-worksheet">Use the quote worksheet</a> · <a href="/pricing/">See CallTeam’s published scope</a></p>
</section>
